From 953b6fd1ebf943e4f9fda72a20b44febaa219fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K11MCH1 <81425424+K11MCH1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:32:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: keep translated code on empty reads and off Wine's
 memory lock

Under Wine, a few FEX paths that are cheap on Linux become calls that take
Wine's global virtual memory lock, and one invalidates far more than it
should:

- After a successful NtReadFile, FEX invalidates translated code in the
  destination buffer. A zero-length read with a NULL buffer, which is how
  programs poll a pipe or a socket, reached InvalidateAlignedInterval with
  address 0, which means the whole process (the FlushInstructionCache(NULL)
  rule). The read notification now returns early for NULL or empty buffers
  and for reads into memory outside FEX's executable intervals, instead of
  taking the code invalidation lock for every data read.
- The code buffer starts at its 128 MB maximum: each growth (16, 32, 64 MB)
  discarded all translated code.
- VirtualDontNeed zeroes memory with MEM_RESET, which Wine turns into one
  madvise, instead of VirtualQuery + decommit + recommit.
- Compiled and linked blocks flush the instruction cache with dc cvau /
  ic ivau, as on Linux, instead of FlushInstructionCache, a system call plus
  FEX's own invalidation callback.
- Executable range lookups ask the OS (VirtualQuery) only for writable
  executable ranges, where a protector can hide inaccessible pages, and on
  misses.
- Opt-in counters (DDO_FEX_DIAG=1 with FEX_SILENTLOG=0) of invalidations by
  source, cache loads, compiles and full code-cache clears, logged every 5 s.

Measured with Dungeons & Dragons Online on a phone: a world load went from
117 s to 54.5 s with the memory paths, and ENTER to in the world from 50 s
to 4.1 s with the read fix; full code-cache clears went from up to 7 per
5 s to none, and the game thread's waits on Wine's virtual_mutex during a
load from 4127 samples to 129.

The rpmalloc half (commit once, never decommit under MinGW) is a separate
patch for External/rpmalloc.
